# Reproducibility and proof coverage

The companion code performs bounded exact-arithmetic sanity checks for a spanning balanced star, a nearest-distance example, a uniform inset on an unbounded face, the saturated covolume ratio, dyadic shifts, and the orthant obstruction inequalities. These are exhaustive finite results only over the explicitly enumerated inputs. The general statements above are mathematical proofs and do not rely on those finite enumerations. No resource-heavy computation was launched; no supervised compute facility was supplied or needed for these proofs.

The build uses local Pandoc and pdfLaTeX with shell escape disabled and captures the first build, its warnings, and subsequent unchanged-source passes. The programs, bounded inputs, outputs, environment report, source-reading log, artifact hashes, full notes, and rerun commands are retained in the fresh artifact directory. No provider nesting, network request, or agent delegation occurs. The visible execution environment is recorded without exposing authentication or runtime configuration. The operator's requested model identity is task metadata, not a separately verifiable backend certificate.

The coverage is: L0 real perspective density and inherited-cell convexity; L1 distance and all-slack insets; L2 real covolume flux and two-sided generator coefficients; L3 finite costs, sublinear envelope, and entire-cell supports; L4 all-face induction and linear constants; L5 scoped regularization input. C1 distance; C2 coercive auxiliary reference; C3 exact full-affine extension; C4 actual-dual full-affine primal majorants; C5 decreasing shifts and finite-contact limits. B1 convexity and recession; B2 the sharp continuum error floor; B3 the boundary-domain diagnosis. None of these coverage labels includes arbitrary shared-face gluing or either complete original classification.

